#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# perfect_number

#% text
# `perfect_number(k)` gives the k-th perfect number, `2^(p - 1) (2^p - 1)` for the k-th Mersenne prime exponent `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is defined for `k` from 1 to 51, the known Mersenne primes; the values grow quickly.

#% item
# Every even perfect number has this form (Euclid, Euler); no odd perfect number is known.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
perfect_number(1)
#% output
#= 6

#% cell
perfect_number(3)
#% output
#= 496

#% cell
table(perfect_number(k), k, 4)
#% output
#= [6, 28, 496, 8128]

#% cell
total(divisors(perfect_number(3))) == 2*perfect_number(3)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `mersenne_prime_exponent`, `divisor_sigma`, `is_prime`
